# GPU firmware shipped in xxri-firmware-gpu.tcz (rules/xxri-firmware-gpu.make).
# Every line is a file the kernel's radeon or i915 driver declares
# (MODULE_FIRMWARE) and requests at probe time; the files come unmodified from
# Tiny Core 16's firmware-radeon.tcz and firmware-i915.tcz (linux-firmware
# 20240220).  Chosen for XXRI's hardware - 32-bit x86 machines, BIOS or
# 32-bit UEFI:
#
#   radeon R100-R500 (Radeon 7000 .. X1950)      CP microcode: acceleration
#   radeon R600-R700 (HD 2000 .. HD 4000, HD 3200/4200 IGPs)  PFP/ME/RLC/SMC
#   radeon Evergreen (HD 5000), Palm/Sumo APUs (E-350/C-50 netbooks, Llano),
#          Northern Islands (HD 6000), Aruba (Trinity/Richland)  PFP/ME/RLC/SMC,
#          and MC for NI - without MC radeon cannot initialise NI at all
#   i915   Gen9 DMC (Skylake, Kaby Lake, Broxton, Gemini Lake): display power
#          states; older Intel GPUs (GMA .. Broadwell, Bay/Cherry Trail) need none
#
# Newer GPUs, up to the 2015-era generations, have extensions of their own
# (linux-firmware 20260810):
#   radeon SI/CIK, amdgpu GCN 3            xxri-firmware-amd.tcz     (amd.list)
#   i915 Atom/Celeron-class Gen11/Gen12    xxri-firmware-intel.tcz   (intel.list)
#   nouveau Maxwell 2                      xxri-firmware-nvidia.tcz  (nvidia.list)
#
# Deliberately not shipped (docs/hardware-issues-2.6.md):
#   radeon UVD/VCE (video decode/encode, ~0.7 MB for these families): nothing
#          in XXRI decodes video on the GPU; radeon runs without them
#   i915 GuC/HuC for Gen9: 6.12's i915 never loads them without
#          enable_guc= (GuC/HuC are default only from Gen12)
#   ast_dp501_fw.bin (server BMC graphics)
